{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":505032,"name":"Brian Miller","username":"Brian_Miller2","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/brian_miller2/{size}/120215_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:53:12.452Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eFor those of you using Vercel hosting and have bots validate their SE work in a branch (using Vercel preview link), how are you handling authentication?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere is \u003ca href=\"https://www.1password.community/1password-at-home-31/support-for-vercel-preview-links-15661/index2.html#post140041\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ea bug with 1Password \u003c/a\u003ecurrently where the preview link is not recognized by 1P, therefore even if you have the credentials saved, it won’t autofill or recognize the credentials being associated with the app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore, even when using the 1P plugin with Grok Bot (in shared with Grok Bot vault), the bot can’t use the shared credentials.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would think this is a very common issue for others given:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMany are using GB for software engineering E2E\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVercel hosting is common\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVercel preview links are used by branches which bots use during development and self validation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMany devs already use 1P\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHaving to manually auth the bot for every task is slowing me down tremendously and kind of defeats the point of agentic development.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow is everyone else solving for credential sharing for SE workflows?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-10-01T21:03:34.739Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":30.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173544,"topic_slug":"1password-vercel-preview-links","display_username":"Brian Miller"